Safety notes:

* Do not remove the compile-time SHA-256 blocker by returning dummy data.
* Cache acknowledgements for duplicate command sequences instead of applying
  the command twice; the RFC codec currently drops duplicates and therefore
  still needs that retry behavior before hardware use.
* Emit partnerPartyReady once per session, not once per subsequent mail word.
* Implement ABORT_IF_SAFE from an explicitly reviewed pre-commit phase.
* The 220-byte mail block remains empty upstream; broker v1 refuses Mail.

